# Privacy Policy

This privacy policy applies to the Pocket Coach AI app for mobile devices, together with any related services operated by Burak Yaman (collectively, the "Application"). Burak Yaman is hereby referred to as the "Service Provider".

## Information Collection and Use

The Application collects information that you provide when you create an account and use it, including:

- Your name and email address
- Your password (stored only in hashed form)
- Your language, timezone and notification time preferences
- Your workout programs, workout logs (exercises, weights, reps, sets, RPE and notes) and weekly goals
- Messages you send to the AI coach, and your feedback (thumbs up/down) on coach replies
- Information the AI coach remembers about you to personalize its guidance, such as your preferences, milestones and any injuries you mention
- Your push notification token, if you allow notifications
- Your subscription status

The Application and its third-party SDKs may also automatically collect information such as:

- Your device's Internet Protocol (IP) address and approximate location derived from it
- Your device type and mobile operating system
- Device identifiers used by the advertising SDK
- Information about how you interact with ads shown in the Application
- Crash and performance diagnostics

## Health and Fitness Data / Medical Disclaimer

The Application collects fitness data you provide (such as workout logs, weights lifted, and fitness goals) and, if you choose to share it with the AI coach, health information such as injuries, in order to generate personalized workout programs and coaching feedback. The Application does not access Apple Health (HealthKit) or any other health data on your device. Your fitness and health data is not used for advertising and is not sold or shared with data brokers. By providing this information, you explicitly consent to the collection and processing of this data for the purpose of personalizing your experience within the Application.

Medical Disclaimer: The workout programs, coaching feedback, and fitness guidance provided by the Application are for informational and educational purposes only and do not constitute medical or professional healthcare advice. The Service Provider is not a licensed medical professional or physician. You should consult with a qualified healthcare provider or physician before starting any new fitness program or exercise regimen, especially if you have pre-existing medical conditions or injuries. You assume full responsibility for any risks, injuries, or damages that may result from your use of or reliance on the fitness information provided by the Application.

## Advertising

The Application offers optional rewarded video ads, provided by Google AdMob, that users on the free plan can watch to earn additional AI coach messages. Ads are requested as non-personalized ads. The Application does not track you across apps and websites owned by other companies and does not request permission to access your device's advertising identifier for tracking. Google may collect certain device and usage information when ads are shown, as described in Google's privacy policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy).

## Cookies and Tracking Technologies

The Application or its third-party SDKs may use SDKs and similar technologies to support functionality, analytics, advertising, or service delivery. Where required by applicable law, the Service Provider will obtain consent before using non-essential tracking technologies.

## Your Rights

You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data held by the Service Provider. You can delete your account and all associated data at any time from within the Application (Settings → Delete Account). To exercise any other rights, or to withdraw consent where processing is based on consent, contact the Service Provider at info@trinexo.io.

## Artificial Intelligence

The Application uses Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies to provide its core features. Specifically, the Application uses Anthropic's Claude API to process the messages you send to the AI coach, together with relevant account and fitness data (such as your name, workout history, goals, and coach memory), in order to generate personalized workout programs, coaching replies, and weekly reviews. Anthropic processes this data on behalf of the Service Provider and, under its commercial terms, does not use it to train its models. All AI processing is performed in accordance with this privacy policy and applicable laws. AI-generated content may be inaccurate; please use your own judgment. If you have questions about the AI features or data processing, please contact the Service Provider.

The Service Provider may use the information you provide to send important information, required notices, workout reminders, and, where permitted by law, marketing communications.

For a better experience while using the Application, the Service Provider may require you to provide certain personally identifiable information. The information the Service Provider requests will be retained and used as described in this privacy policy.

## Third Party Access

The Service Provider does not sell your personal data. The Service Provider may share your information with third parties in the ways that are described in this privacy statement, including the following service providers used by the Application:

- **Anthropic (Claude API)**, to generate AI coach replies, personalized workout programs, and weekly reviews
- **Google AdMob**, to show optional rewarded video ads
- **RevenueCat**, to manage in-app subscriptions
- **Apple App Store / Google Play**, to process in-app purchases and manage subscriptions
- **Expo (Expo Push Notification Service)**, to deliver push notifications
- **Sentry**, to monitor server errors and improve reliability

## International Data Transfers

The Service Provider or its third-party service providers may transfer personal data to countries outside your country of residence, including outside the European Economic Area (EEA). Where applicable law requires safeguards for international transfers, the Service Provider will use appropriate mechanisms, such as:

- Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved by the European Commission
- Adequacy decisions or other legally recognized transfer mechanisms
- Your consent, where required and legally permitted

Data protection laws in other countries may differ from those in your jurisdiction. Where required by law, the Service Provider will apply appropriate safeguards and obtain any consent required for the transfer.

The Service Provider may disclose User Provided and Automatically Collected Information:

- as required by law, such as to comply with a subpoena, or similar legal process;
- when they believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary to protect their rights, protect your safety or the safety of others, investigate fraud, or respond to a government request;
- with their trusted services providers who work on their behalf, do not have an independent use of the information the Service Provider discloses to them, and have agreed to adhere to the rules set forth in this privacy statement.

## Opt-Out Rights

You can stop further collection of information from your mobile device by uninstalling the Application. Uninstalling will stop the Application from collecting data from your device, but it does not automatically delete information that has already been transmitted to the Service Provider or to third parties. You can turn off push notifications at any time in your device settings.

To delete your personal data, use the Delete Account option in the Application, or contact the Service Provider at info@trinexo.io.

## Data Retention Policy

The Service Provider retains personal data based on its necessity for the stated purposes:

- User Provided Data: Retained for as long as your account is active. When you delete your account, this data is deleted immediately.
- Automatically Collected Data: Retained for up to 24 months from collection, unless longer retention is required for legal compliance
- Aggregated and Anonymized Data: Retained indefinitely as it no longer identifies you
- Data required for legal compliance: Retained as long as required by applicable law

Third-party service providers may retain data according to their own policies. For details, see our Account Deletion policy.

## Children

The Application is not intended for children under 13 years of age, or such higher age as required by applicable law. The Service Provider does not knowingly solicit data from children or market the Application to them.

The Service Provider does not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children. The Service Provider encourages all children to never submit any personally identifiable information through the Application and/or Services. The Service Provider encourages parents and legal guardians to monitor their children's Internet usage and to help enforce this Policy by instructing their children never to provide personally identifiable information through the Application and/or Services without their permission. If you have reason to believe that a child has provided personally identifiable information to the Service Provider through the Application and/or Services, please contact the Service Provider so that they will be able to take the necessary actions. If you are under the age of digital consent in your country, your parent or guardian must provide consent on your behalf where required by law.

## Security

The Service Provider is concerned about safeguarding the confidentiality of your information. The Service Provider provides physical, electronic, and procedural safeguards to protect information the Service Provider processes and maintains. Data is transmitted over encrypted connections (HTTPS), passwords are stored in hashed form, and authentication tokens are stored in your device's secure storage.

## Data Breach Notification

If a data breach occurs that affects your personal data, the Service Provider will notify you in accordance with applicable legal requirements, including, where required, providing information about the nature of the breach and the steps being taken to address it.

## Changes

The Service Provider may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The Service Provider will notify you of material changes by posting the updated Privacy Policy with an effective date. Where required by law, the Service Provider will seek your consent to material changes before they take effect.

Previous versions of this Privacy Policy will be maintained and made available upon request by contacting the Service Provider at info@trinexo.io.

